of vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"supplies more than its out-edges carry. Costs may be negative, and negative cycles are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"saturated. A self-loop carries its capacity when its cost is negative and nothing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"otherwise. Capacities may be of an unsigned type, up to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int.max"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Computed by the network simplex with block-search pivots and strongly feasible trees."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Which optimum is returned when several exist is unspecified, but the same input always"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"gives the same result. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"supply"},{"type":"text","text":" is called once per vertex in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order, then, for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each edge in position order, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"capacity"},{"type":"text","text":" and then "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cost"},{"type":"text","text":", before any work."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every capacity is at least zero; capacities, supplies and costs fit in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":"; Σ capacity × |cost| fits in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Cost"},{"type":"text","text":" (checked before solving, since it bounds the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"total cost); 4(n + 1)(the greatest |cost| of a non-loop edge + 1) fits in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" (the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"solver’s artificial cost, with room for its potentials and reduced costs); the positive"},{"type":"text","text":" "},